    "rawText": "[SongTitle: Static Turns to Dawn]\r\n[Style: alternative rock, cinematic hybrid, clean studio recording, expressive male vocal]\r\n[Caption: Noise settles, direction appears.]\r\n[Image: Faded horizon clearing into sharp morning light.]\r\n[Refresh Title: Early Morning Walk]\r\n[Theme: Sky]\r\n[Gradients: 4]\r\n[Rank: 33]\r\n[TitleRarityPct: 2.19]\r\n[Seeds: 682, A:47, B:87, C:35, D:21]\r\n[Composer Version: v2.0]\r\n\r\n[Plan]\r\n[Perspective: i_reflect]\r\n[Concept: Finding calm motion after restless noise.]\r\n[Topic: Sky & Perspective → storm_then_clear]\r\n[GenreBias: alternative rock]\r\n[StyleChange: none]\r\n[Modulation: none]\r\n[HookProminence: medium]\r\n[Deviation: none]\r\n\r\n[Intro]\r\n[MelodicConcept: long-tone release]\r\nMorning hums behind my eyes,\r\nGrey light stretching through the lines.\r\n\r\n[Verse]\r\n[MelodicConcept: conversational contour]\r\nI walked with static in my head,\r\nEvery thought half-born, half-said.\r\nThe street was quiet, breath held thin,\r\nLike it knew the day would bend.\r\n\r\n[Verse]\r\n[MelodicConcept: stepwise triad stairs]\r\nEach step aligned my pace with time,\r\nCracks in concrete, beat by beat.\r\nThe noise fell off, a coat of night,\r\nLeft at the corner of the street.\r\n\r\n[Bridge]\r\n[MelodicConcept: asymmetric phrasing]\r\nClouds pulled back without a sound,\r\nThe city softened, slowed me down.\r\nNo sudden truth, no grand reveal,\r\nJust space enough to breathe and feel.\r\n\r\n[Chorus]\r\n[MelodicConcept: call-and-answer hook]\r\nAnd I’m clear now, clearer than before,\r\nThe sky repeats what I ignored.\r\nI’m clear now, standing in the calm,\r\nNothing missing, nothing wrong.\r\n\r\n[Final Chorus]\r\n[MelodicConcept: register swap]\r\nI’m clear now, daylight on my skin,\r\nThe quiet lets the signal in.\r\nI’m clear now, hear the morning say,\r\nYou don’t need more to start the day.\r\n\r\n[Ending]\r\n[MelodicConcept: gentle sequence]\r\nThe road goes on, the doubt is gone,\r\nStatic 